+# The allow list of the time gate of the tests in tests/it (ADR-t1707-1).
+# `sh scripts/check-it-test-time.sh` fails when a test of dagq::it that the
+# diff added or changed took longer than the threshold in the nextest output
+# and has no item here. The threshold, the format and the naming rule are in
+# docs/design/slow-tests.md, section "itのtestの時間の関門", and the rule on
+# which reasons may put a test here in docs/development/testing.md, section
+# "判断と境界のtest". The script reads this file (CI and the worker run it).
+#
+# Each item is one [[test]] with all three keys:
+#
+# [[test]]
+# name = "runtime_handoff::review_verdicts::reviews_that_ended_before_the_exec_are_applied_not_run_again"
+# reason = "the boundary it keeps, or the move it waits for and the goal or task that does it"
+# task = 1707          # the task that put the item here
+#
+# name is the full nextest name of the test in the binary dagq::it, mods and
+# all; an item with the fn's name alone allows nothing.
+#
+# The first items (task 1707): every dagq::it test whose median over the ten
+# latest production gate logs with a Summary (2026-10-04T20:32 to
+# 2026-10-05T00:06 +0900) was over 5 seconds, as summed by
+# scripts/slow-tests.sh. The class and the reason come from
+# docs/plans/it-reduction/it-tests.tsv (task 1706) when its module and test
+# columns match the name's first and last parts in exactly one row, and the
+# class is unknown otherwise. The comment above an item gives the median.
+
